Id: con021c
Severity: CONFIG
Category: tigris
Check: find_files
References: tigris.conf; find(1)

The file system scan left a file system out because the configuration
says so. Tigris_FSScan_SkipTypes names file system types and
Tigris_FSScan_SkipMounts names mount points; a file system of such a
type, one mounted at such a path, and any file system mounted below
such a path is not walked at all: no setuid or setgid programs, device
files, world-writable files or directories, unowned files or dangling
links are looked for on it. The message names the file system, its type
and the setting that left it out.

Auditing a system that is not running (tigris --root), the scan has no
mount table of that system, and Tigris_FSScan_SkipMounts names its
directories instead: the message then says which directory of the root
was not walked.

This is the arrangement for a large data disk or a backup volume, where
a scan takes hours and finds nothing a system audit is about. It is
reported on every run so that a report never passes for a scan of
everything. If the file system should be scanned after all, take its
type or its mount point out of the setting in the tigris.conf or the
profile.
